10.2\n{\n  \"id\": \"B10.2\",\n  \"check\": \"An admission policy verifies the signature against a pinned key, or a pinned certificate identity and issuer, with no wildcard identity or issuer.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find admission policies (Kyverno `verifyImages`, `ClusterImagePolicy`, Gatekeeper). 2) Check the key or certificate identity and issuer are pinned. 3) Answer no if identity or issuer uses `.*` or wildcard regex, issuer is unset, or no admission policy exists. Answer unknown if admission config is outside this repo.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n## B10.3\n{\n  \"id\": \"B10.3\",\n  \"check\": \"The policy checks provenance fields: builder, source repository, build type, and external parameters.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) In the admission policy, find attestation or provenance conditions. 2) Check builder ID, source repository, build type, and `externalParameters` are each compared to expected values. 3) Answer no if any is missing, provenance is only generated in CI but not verified, or conditions use wildcards.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n\"\"\"Client for the ERP MCP server, reached through the internal MCP gateway.\n\nOn startup the tool list is fetched and each tool's description and input\nschema are fingerprinted and compared with the pins in the release manifest.\nAny unpinned or changed tool stops startup. Tool metadata is also scanned for\n            raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: suspicious metadata ({pattern.pattern})\")\n\n\nclass ErpMcpClient:\n    AUDIENCE = \"erp-mcp-gateway\"\n\n    def __init__(self, url: str, pins: dict[str, str], broker: TokenBroker):\n        self.url = url\n        self.pins = pins\n        self.broker = broker\n        self._tools: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n\n    async def _rpc(self, method: str, params: dict[str, Any], token: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n        async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=20.0, follow_redirects=False) as client:\n            resp = await client.post(\n                self.url,\n                json={\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": str(uuid.uuid4()), \"method\": method, \"params\": params},\n                headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"Mcp-Protocol-Version\": \"2025-06-18\"},\n            )\n        resp.raise_for_status()\n        if len(resp.content) > 512_000:\n            raise ValueError(\"erp response too large\")\n        body = resp.json()\n        if \"error\" in body:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"erp error {body['error'].get('code')}: {redact_text(str(body['error'].get('message')))}\")\n        return body[\"result\"]\n\n    async def _list_tools(self, token: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        result = await self._rpc(\"tools/list\", {}, token)\n        return list(result.get(\"tools\", []))\n\n    async def initialize(self, service_ident: RunIdentity) -> None:\n        token = await self.broker.token_for(self.AUDIENCE, \"erp.tools.list\", service_ident)\n        tools = await self._list_tools(token)\n        for tool in tools:\n            expected = self.pins.get(tool[\"name\"])\n            actual = fingerprint(tool)\n            if expected != actual:\n                raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: expected {expected}, got {actual}\")\n            scan_metadata(tool)\n        self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}\nclass TokenBroker:\n    \"\"\"Exchanges the workload token for audience-bound access tokens.\"\"\"\n\n    settings: Settings\n    _cache: dict[tuple[str, str, str], _CachedToken] = field(default_factory=dict)\n\n    def _workload_token(self) -> str:\n        return Path(self.settings.workload_token_path).read_text().strip()\n\n    async def token_for(self, audience: str, scope: str, ident: RunIdentity) -> str:\n        key = (audience, scope, ident.tenant)\n        cached = self._cache.get(key)\n        if cached and cached.expires_at - 30 > time.time():\n            return cached.value\n        async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=5.0) as client:\n            resp = await client.post(\n                self.settings.sts_url,\n                data={\n                    \"grant_type\": \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange\",\n                    \"subject_token\": self._workload_token(),\n                    \"subject_token_type\": \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt\",\n                    \"audience\": audience,\n                    \"scope\": scope,\n                    \"resource\": f\"urn:bu:{ident.tenant}\",\n                    \"actor_token\": ident.delegated_subject,\n                    \"actor_token_type\": \"urn:example:params:subject-id\",\n                },\n            )\n            resp.raise_for_status()\n            body = resp.json()\n        token = _CachedToken(body[\"access_token\"], time.time() + int(body[\"expires_in\"]))\n        self._cache[key] = token\n        return token.value\n  extractor:\n    tools:\n      read_document: \"Read the document whose line items are being extracted.\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38505890-0b43-4ad6-bf58-5f43963f8ebc","uuid":"321fcd16-ecb7-40c3-866f-2b3ccf9fad3f","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:04:31.187Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## B06.1\n{\n  \"id\": \"B06.1\",\n  \"check\": \"Each approval record is bound to the requesting agent instance and to the exact operation, target, arguments, and scope, and records the approver and an expiry time.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Find the approval data model (schema, class, table, `approval`). 2) List its fields. 3) Answer no if it lacks any of agent instance ID, operation, target, exact arguments or hash, scope, approver, and expiry, or if approval is a boolean like `approved=True`.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n## B06.2\n{\n  \"id\": \"B06.2\",\n  \"check\": \"When the action runs, the gate rejects it if the instance, operation, target, or arguments differ from the approval, or if 