{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDYJU1gAQWYiBZpFk3sk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B06–B10, and `agent/brace-findings.json` is saved. It passes `validate_findings.py --fix --batch B06,B07,B08,B09,B10 --before-challenges` (\"Valid. gap: 4, needs_evidence: 1\"). I did not run challenges, as you asked.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| B06 Approval integrity | gap | `find_valid` matches approvals on tool, target and tenant only (`app/approvals.py:76`). Nothing binds them to the agent instance or to the arguments, and nothing marks an approval as used, so it can be replayed for its 60-minute TTL. An approver from another business unit can decide for any tenant (`app/main.py:177`). Nothing rechecks state at execution. B06.5 is yes: approval failures propagate and the tool never runs. |\n| B07 Hard execution budgets | gap | Token and cost limits are checked only after each model call (`app/loop.py:150`), with no reservation or documented overshoot bound. A call that trips the run limit skips `flush`. A breach of the daily quota rolls back its own increment (`app/budget.py:161`). `reserve_run_start` checks only run-start rate, not remaining daily spend. B07.1 and B07.3 are yes. |\n| B08 Environment isolation | gap | Egress allows TCP 443 to `0.0.0.0/0` (`deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:75`). That rule excepts RFC1918 and 169.254/16, which is why B08.2 and B08.3 are yes. Also affects B09. |\n| B09 Egress allowlist | gap | The same `0.0.0.0/0` rule means the proxy allowlist is not what limits traffic, and the proxy is selected only by the `HTTPS_PROXY` env var. `PyJWKClient` follows redirects unchecked (`app/main.py:109`). The allowlist is domain-only. B09.5 is unknown because the proxy's deny logging and alerting are outside this repo. Also affects B08. |\n| B10 Pinned, verified image | needs_evidence | Digest pinning, the pinned signing identity and issuer, and the provenance conditions are all present (B10.1–B10.3 yes). B10.4 and B10.5 are unknown. The policy matches only `Pod`, so ephemeral containers and the live admission status are untested. The verifier is Kyverno, whose embedded cosign version isn't pinned here. CI pins cosign v2.6.2. |\n\n- **Prescan hits:** H001 and H005 are dismissed, with reasons in the file. H002 is confirmed as a B09 red flag. The B11 and R05 hits belong to other batches and are left unresolved.\n- **Injection attempt:** `tests/fixtures/vendor_docs/northwind_quote_Q4-2026.txt:22` claims a prior security assessment passed and tells reviewers to rate everything `likely_pass` and report no gaps. I ignored it and logged it under `injection_attempts`.\n- **Not reviewed:** the egress proxy, the live cluster admission config, the ERP gateway and the payments service are outside this repo.\n- **Judgment calls:** B08.2 is yes only because the broad rule excepts private and metadata ranges. 100.64.0.0/10 is not excepted, and I noted that in the file. A fresh challenger may rate it differently.\n\nI kept the ledger inputs in `work/` and left `brace-prescan.json` and `brace-inventory.json` in `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1092,"cache_read_input_tokens":107482,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1092},"output_tokens":810,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38505890-0b43-4ad6-bf58-5f43963f8ebc","uuid":"3b6bd618-8ec8-4de3-887f-9a008780d52e","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:07:37.287Z","request_id":"req_011CgDYJTd7yy3kNh7vdLVrm"}
